#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046644} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511645} :activity/id #uuid "2e6736bd-345f-5eb1-b1d1-69bf9d392abd" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049041 :topic/id #uuid "d56dd46d-c76b-5160-925e-c4ddd2d90833" :topic/math-academy-id 3354} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511593 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259520 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19e0accf-355f-56fb-b473-52acb69bd23b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{7\\pi /6}\\sqrt{10+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta +12{sin}^{2}⁡4\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257002} {:answer/id #uuid "1a282cf9-e726-5893-9709-a1869d24dfa0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{7\\pi /6}\\sqrt{17+8\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta +15{sin}^{2}⁡4\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257005} {:answer/id #uuid "58bdd781-32a3-5cea-bf8a-eda0cdb4360a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{7\\pi /6}\\sqrt{12+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta +10{sin}^{2}⁡4\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257551} {:answer/id #uuid "7d2de95a-65cf-5b52-864b-9114a600f1ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{7\\pi /6}\\sqrt{12+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta +8{sin}^{2}⁡4\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257887} {:answer/id #uuid "d1432cc5-bba9-5179-80ef-98471b08f92d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{7\\pi /6}\\sqrt{4+8\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta +12{sin}^{2}⁡4\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258605}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186257005} :answer-field/id #uuid "7adf0afe-c0b4-5de7-8baf-d650968a622b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259239}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "77c73302-f62f-524d-b1a1-cbae03250f18" :question/math-academy-id "q-123395" :question/problem "![](images/7d/7dc83cbf45ec3025ad33552ce889c7ecb2daf73b426bc2fd10ec932f3311c92a.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r=4+\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta \\,$ for $-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{7\\pi }{6},$ shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=4+\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expression for our line integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{7\\pi /6}\\sqrt{(4+\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta )^{2}+(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta )^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{7\\pi /6}\\sqrt{16+8\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡4\\theta +16{sin}^{2}⁡4\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{7\\pi /6}\\sqrt{16+8\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta +1+15{sin}^{2}⁡4\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{7\\pi /6}\\sqrt{17+8\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta +15{sin}^{2}⁡4\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "19f4932e-c75d-5c67-b1d4-b8ff2197751a" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511661}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511645 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259519 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bd7e7ed-0cb5-5f2a-9906-20fa4a290dec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{5-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256894} {:answer/id #uuid "22a84c4e-ebcd-5545-8a90-d6cd63c6a644" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{5+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257070} {:answer/id #uuid "3b6fff17-f37b-5bca-8413-fcf9937009c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{5-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257313} {:answer/id #uuid "785374b9-120b-5f1f-a6e2-69129997ff6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{5-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257847} {:answer/id #uuid "b514f795-53a7-5471-a8c9-56185b112376" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{4-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258354}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256894} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe556346-c85f-5997-afb5-d4236fb40204" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259479}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f4d5a329-2172-581a-b274-24fd141bca53" :question/math-academy-id "q-123371" :question/problem "![](images/5b/5b6490495c297b49d394b0f7c494fb35b710c8c4520ab898783877abdd079013.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r=2-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,$ for $\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\pi ,$ shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=2-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expression for our line integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{(2-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{4-16\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +16{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +16{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{4-16\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +16}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{20-16\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{5-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "9df4f53a-cfc3-5f5d-9dd3-d0e7ba431674" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511593}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511657 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511492 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d3de7cb-dc94-55e8-a78d-a27f24ecf883" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{\\pi }\\frac{\\sqrt{{\\theta }^{4}+1}}{{\\theta }^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510875} {:answer/id #uuid "5df30dae-9f1b-5169-85f4-352ef7b35830" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{\\pi }\\frac{\\sqrt{{\\theta }^{2}+1}}{2\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510978} {:answer/id #uuid "8b872d30-3b7e-5aae-91f8-0a201257e3ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{\\pi }\\frac{\\sqrt{{\\theta }^{2}+1}}{{\\theta }^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511071} {:answer/id #uuid "c81c2c1a-18d2-5fae-8d05-046e1ef9709a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{\\pi }\\frac{\\sqrt{\\theta }}{\\theta +1}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511197} {:answer/id #uuid "f3baf0b1-8376-594a-b0c2-adace7164539" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{\\pi }\\frac{2\\sqrt{\\theta }}{{\\theta }^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511287}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511071} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ddef5b4-7fd6-526e-90d2-54235e050d54" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511337}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4cb23656-32ad-5111-abf0-812956e034d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-149800" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r=\\frac{1}{\\theta }$ for $1\\le \\theta \\le \\pi \\,?$" :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=\\frac{1}{\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=-\\frac{1}{{\\theta }^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expression for our line integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{(\\frac{1}{\\theta })}^{2}+{(-\\frac{1}{{\\theta }^{2}})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{{\\theta }^{2}}+\\frac{1}{{\\theta }^{4}}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{\\frac{{\\theta }^{2}+1}{{\\theta }^{4}}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\pi }\\frac{\\sqrt{{\\theta }^{2}+1}}{{\\theta }^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "b40a5a22-c678-5bc6-8e83-8d3a7d00ab97"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511661 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511546 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01eaff75-9bd9-584b-8dac-798d298e7fe1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2({e}^{\\pi /4}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510777} {:answer/id #uuid "0d033828-6617-5a30-b0e6-4a3c14d14576" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510806} {:answer/id #uuid "19428a95-6f1a-515e-aa64-ad5b042f4aa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}{e}^{\\pi /4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510840} {:answer/id #uuid "51635b1e-3cd9-5e5e-8da8-a31c41a6b5bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2{e}^{\\pi /4}({e}^{\\pi /4}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510956} {:answer/id #uuid "e233503b-2829-57e2-afff-b160c60d6d3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /4}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511251}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510956} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2bc4d54-53d7-5960-8596-76e1189178c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511417}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "b688c283-ffe1-5279-a25b-e224f4238243" :question/math-academy-id "q-123634" :question/problem "Calculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r=\\sqrt{2}\\,{e}^{\\theta }\\,$ for $\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=\\sqrt{2}{e}^{\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=\\sqrt{2}\\,{e}^{\\theta }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we evaluate our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{(\\sqrt{2}\\,{e}^{\\theta })}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{2}\\,{e}^{\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{2{e}^{2\\theta }+2{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{4{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}2{e}^{\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{e}^{\\theta }{|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =2({e}^{\\pi /2}-{e}^{\\pi /4}) \\\\  & =2{e}^{\\pi /4}({e}^{\\pi /4}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "ca26c44a-47b3-5082-aab1-eac96843df54" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511675}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511675 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511541 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "051f2eaa-30f6-5a12-9a77-9f95ac0b3e71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510788} {:answer/id #uuid "3257bf5c-fa92-5d61-948f-9e8f3c674e46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510889} {:answer/id #uuid "5896cb3f-bb8d-57b4-adca-c7ec3f6be4d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510970} {:answer/id #uuid "bda1540c-a5f2-5558-ad30-970a0713c6a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511174} {:answer/id #uuid "dba7e57b-8972-5648-baf2-34e857e37757" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511235}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510788} :answer-field/id #uuid "99e9e8ce-81b5-5865-823b-16944100d9f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511393}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "acde0039-9e1f-5668-bb5b-a5df57c98611" :question/math-academy-id "q-123643" :question/problem "Calculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r=\\sqrt{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta }\\,$ for $\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\pi .$" :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=\\sqrt{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta }\\,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta }{\\sqrt{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta }}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we evaluate our line integral as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{(\\sqrt{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta })^{2}+{(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta }{\\sqrt{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta }})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta )+\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡2\\theta }{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{\\frac{(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta )^{2}+{cos}^{2}⁡2\\theta }{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{\\frac{1-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡2\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡2\\theta }{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{\\frac{2-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta }{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\,\\theta {|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\text{ }(\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id 